  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5421",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the regulation of KYSE-140 through multiple distinct pathways. The drug targets bromodomain-containing protein 4, which is a target of patupilone and ultimately affects KYSE-140. Similarly, palmarumycin CP18 also targets A704, a compound that is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn affects KYSE-140. These pathways suggest that palmarumycin CP18 exerts its effects through different molecular mechanisms that ultimately lead to the inhibition of KYSE-140. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of target engagement across different molecular entities, indicating a potential role in modulating cellular processes that influence the growth or survival of KYSE-140 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the drug's action, with each target contributing to a broader biological effect on the cancer cell line.",
